0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   1   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
                    BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
                    BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
0000                             ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000                LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
0000                SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                          .ORG   BASE   
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0000                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0000                          IF   1-EDGEN   
                              LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000   AF                     XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
0001   32 00 83               LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
0004   C3 75 04               JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
0007   00                     NOP      ; 07  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   start   ; 03
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                VECS:        
0008                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0008   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0009   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
000A   23                     INC   HL   
000B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
000C   23                     INC   HL   
000D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
000E   D9                     EXX      
000F   D1                     POP   DE   
0010   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0011                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0011   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0013   20 1C                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0015   C3 BD 04     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0018                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0018   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0019   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
001A   18 15                  JR   nx   
001C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
001D   CF                     RST   08h   
001E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
001F   F7                     RST   30h   
0020                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0020   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0021   95                     SUB   L   
0022   6F                     LD   L,A   
0023   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0024   94                     SUB   H   
0025   67                     LD   H,A   
0026   C9                     RET      
0027   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0028                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0028                RST28:       
0028                          IFN   CPM   
0028   C3 03 FF     PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   putc   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
002C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
002D   C3 B7 00               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0030                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0030   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0031                NX:          
0031                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0031                          ENDIF      
0031                VECEND:      
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0031                             ; 
0031                             ;    00h          end of program
0031                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0031                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0031                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0031                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0031                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                NEXT0:       
0031                          IF   CHECKED   
0031   CD 3E 03               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0034                          ENDIF      
0034   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0035   03                     INC   BC   
0036   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0038   38 D7                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
003A   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
003C   38 25                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
003E   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0040   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0042   38 5D                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0044   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0046   38 19                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0048   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
004A   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
004C   38 5F                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
004E   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0050   38 0D                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0052   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0054   38 51                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0056   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
0058                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0058                          ENDIF      
0058                          IF   CHECKED   
0058   28 D7                  JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
005A   D2 6B 03               JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
005D                          ENDIF      
005D   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
005F   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0061   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0063                .macro PTABLE,
0063                             ; 
0063                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0063                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0063                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0063                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0063                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0063                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0063                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0063                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0063                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0063                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0063                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0063                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0063                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0063                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0063                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0063                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0063                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0063                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0063                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0063                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0063                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0063                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0063                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0063                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0063                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0063                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0063                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0063                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0063                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0063                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0063                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0063                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0063                .endm
0063                 
0063                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0063                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0063   C6 AD        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0065   5F                     LD   E,A   
0066   16 02                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
0068   FE C3                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
006A   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
006B   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
006C                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
006C   16 00                  LD   D,0   
006E                          ENDIF      
006E                          IFN   CPM   
006E   CB 12                  RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
0070                          ENDIF      
0070                          IF   CPM   
                              LD   D,1   
                              JR   NC,pu1   
                              INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
                    PU1:         
0070                          ENDIF      
0070   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0071   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0072                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0072                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0072                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0072                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0072                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0072                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0072                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
0072                          ENDIF      ;   these)
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
                              LD   HL,0   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
0072                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
0072                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
0072                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                             ; =============================================================================
0072                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0072                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
0072                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
0072                             ; =============================================================================
0072   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0073   7C                     LD   A,H   
0074   AA                     XOR   D   
0075   67                     LD   H,A   
0076   7D                     LD   A,L   
0077   AB                     XOR   E   
0078   6F                     LD   L,A   
0079   F7                     RST   30h   
007A   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
007B   7C                     LD   A,H   
007C   B2                     OR   D   
007D   67                     LD   H,A   
007E   7D                     LD   A,L   
007F   B3                     OR   E   
0080   6F                     LD   L,A   
0081   F7                     RST   30h   
0082   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0083   2B                     DEC   HL   
0084   F7                     RST   30h   
0085                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0085                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0085   ED 5B 7C 82  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
0089                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
0089                          ENDIF      
0089   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
008A                          IF   CHECKED   
008A   CD 2A 03               CALL   chkhp   
008D                          ENDIF      
008D   22 7C 82               LD   (HEAP),HL   
0090   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0091   F7                     RST   30h   
0092   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
0093   22 34 82               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
0096   D9                     EXX      
0097   CD 2B 00               CALL   jphl   
009A   D9                     EXX      
009B   2A 34 82               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
009E   D9                     EXX      
009F   E1                     POP   HL   
00A0   F7                     RST   30h   
00A1                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
00A1                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
00A1                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
00A1   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
00A2   0B                     DEC   BC   
00A3   CD 2F 02               CALL   rdnum   
00A6   F7                     RST   30h   
00A7                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
00A7   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
00A8   87                     ADD   A,A   
00A9   6F                     LD   L,A   
00AA   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
00AC   F7                     RST   30h   
00AD                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
00AD                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
00AD   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
00AE   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
00AF   87                     ADD   A,A   
00B0   6F                     LD   L,A   
00B1   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
00B3   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
00B4   2C                     INC   L   
00B5   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
00B6   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
00B7                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
00B7                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
00B7                             ; 
00B7                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
00B7                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
00B7                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
00B7                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
00B7                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
00B7                             ; both ways out.)
00B7   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
00B8   D1                     POP   DE   
00B9   2B                     DEC   HL   
00BA   72                     LD   (HL),D   
00BB   2B                     DEC   HL   
00BC   73                     LD   (HL),E   
00BD   05                     DEC   B   
00BE   D9                     EXX      
00BF   CC DF 02               CALL   Z,pollk   
00C2   F7                     RST   30h   
00C3                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
00C3                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
00C3                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
00C3                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
00C3                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
00C3                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
00C3                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
00C3   CD CD 02     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
00C6   30 CA                  JR   NC,exec   
00C8   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
00C9   CD CD 02               CALL   hexc   
00CC   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
00CE   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
00D0   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
00D1   CD CD 02               CALL   hexc   
00D4   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
00D6   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
00D8   F7                     RST   30h   
00D9                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
00D9                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
00D9                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
00D9                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
00D9                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
00D9                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
00D9   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
00DA   42                     LD   B,D   
00DB   4B                     LD   C,E   
00DC   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
00DD                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
00DD                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
00DD   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
00DE   B5                     OR   L   
00DF   E1                     POP   HL   
00E0   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
00E2   CD 56 02               CALL   skip   
00E5   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
00E6   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
00E8   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
00E9   F7                     RST   30h   
00EA                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
00EA                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
00EA                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
00EA                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
00EA                             ; checked build stops on it.)
00EA   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
00EB   03                     INC   BC   
00EC   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
00EE   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
00EF   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
00F1   FE 1A                  CP   26   
00F3   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
00F5   CB 23                  SLA   E   
00F7   16 82                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
00F9   79                     LD   A,C   
00FA   12                     LD   (DE),A   
00FB   1C                     INC   E   
00FC   78                     LD   A,B   
00FD   12                     LD   (DE),A   
00FE   18 09                  JR   skipnx   
0100                DEF2:        
0100                          IF   CHECKED   
0100   7B                     LD   A,E   
0101   FE DF                  CP   " "-"A"+256   
0103   C2 8B 03               JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0106                          ENDIF      
0106   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0107   60                     LD   H,B   
0108   69                     LD   L,C   
0109                SKIPNX:      
0109                          IF   CHECKED   
0109   0B                     DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
010A                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
010A   CD 56 02     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
010D   F7                     RST   30h   
010E   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
010F   23                     INC   HL   
0110   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0111   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0112   F7                     RST   30h   
0113                             ; =============================================================================
0113                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0113                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0113                             ;  page.
0113                             ; =============================================================================
0113                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0113                             ; the matching ")".
0113   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0114   B5                     OR   L   
0115   E1                     POP   HL   
0116   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
0118   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
0119   18 9C                  JR   rpushn   
011B                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
011B                             ; drops it and carries on.
011B   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
011C   B5                     OR   L   
011D   E1                     POP   HL   
011E   28 C8                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0120   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0121   42                     LD   B,D   
0122   4B                     LD   C,E   
0123   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0124   18 91                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0126                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0126                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0126   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
0127   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0129   FE 0A                  CP   10   
012B   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
012D   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
012E   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
012F   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0130   F7                     RST   30h   
0131   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0132   CD 2F 02               CALL   rdnum   
0135   E7                     RST   20h   
0136   F7                     RST   30h   
0137   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
0138   7C                     LD   A,H   
0139   A2                     AND   D   
013A   67                     LD   H,A   
013B   7D                     LD   A,L   
013C   A3                     AND   E   
013D   6F                     LD   L,A   
013E   F7                     RST   30h   
013F                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
013F                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
013F                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
013F                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
013F   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0140   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0141   7C                     LD   A,H   
0142   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0144   67                     LD   H,A   
0145   7A                     LD   A,D   
0146   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0148   57                     LD   D,A   
0149   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
014B   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
014D   F7                     RST   30h   
014E   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
014F   B7                     OR   A   
0150   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0152   7C                     LD   A,H   
0153   B5                     OR   L   
0154   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0156   18 F3                  JR   tf   
0158                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
0158                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
0158   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
0159   C5                     PUSH   BC   
015A   7C                     LD   A,H   
015B   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
015C   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
015F   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0161   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0162   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0164   17                     RLA      
0165   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
0167   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0168   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
016A   C1                     POP   BC   
016B   F7                     RST   30h   
016C                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
016C                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
016C                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
016C                             ; stops on it.
016C                H_DIV:       
016C                          IF   CHECKED   
016C   7C                     LD   A,H   
016D   B5                     OR   L   
016E   CA 88 03               JP   Z,e_zero   
0171                          ENDIF      
0171   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0172   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
0173   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0174   7A                     LD   A,D   
0175   AC                     XOR   H   
0176   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0177   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0179   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
017C   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
017D   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
017F   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0182   CD 09 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0185   F1                     POP   AF   
0186   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0189   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
018A   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
018B   B7                     OR   A   
018C   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
018F   C1                     POP   BC   
0190   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
0191   F7                     RST   30h   
0192                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
0192   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
0193   F7                     RST   30h   
0194   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
0195   F7                     RST   30h   
0196                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
0196                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
0196                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
0196                          IF   CHECKED   
0196   CD 1D 03               CALL   chkst   
0199                          ENDIF      
0199   D1                     POP   DE   
019A   73                     LD   (HL),E   
019B   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
019C                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
019C                          IF   CHECKED   
019C   CD 1D 03               CALL   chkst   
019F                          ENDIF      
019F   D1                     POP   DE   
01A0   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01A1   23                     INC   HL   
01A2   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01A3   DF                     RST   18h   
01A4                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
01A4                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
01A4   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
01A5   60                     LD   H,B   
01A6   69                     LD   L,C   
01A7   CD 45 02               CALL   skipstr   
01AA                          IF   CHECKED   
01AA   B7                     OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
01AB   CA 80 03               JP   Z,e_quote   
01AE                          ENDIF      
01AE   F7                     RST   30h   
01AF                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
01AF                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
01AF                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
01AF                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
01AF                          ENDIF      
01AF                          IF   CHECKED   
01AF                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
01AF                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
01AF                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
01AF   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
01B0   CD 4F 04               CALL   prstr   
01B3   D1                     POP   DE   
01B4   DF                     RST   18h   
01B5                          ENDIF      
01B5                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                                 ; (With the editor the loop is a routine, prstr, which ^V uses too.)
                    H_PRINT:   CALL   prstr   
                              RST   18h   
01B5                          ENDIF      
01B5   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
01B6   EF                     RST   28h   
01B7   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
01B8                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
01B8   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
01B9   CD 93 02               CALL   psgn   
01BC   C1                     POP   BC   
01BD   DF                     RST   18h   
01BE                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
01BE                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
01BE                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
01BE                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
01BE                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
01BE   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
01C0   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
01C2   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
01C4   CD 0D 03     KT2:      CALL   getk   
01C7   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
01C9   1D                     DEC   E   
01CA   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
01CC   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
01CD   B5                     OR   L   
01CE   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
01D0   2B                     DEC   HL   
01D1   7C                     LD   A,H   
01D2   B5                     OR   L   
01D3   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
01D5   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
01D6   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
01D7   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
01D8   26 00                  LD   H,0   
01DA   F7                     RST   30h   
01DB                          IF   CPM   
                                 ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
                                 ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
                              LD   (LBHDR),A   
                              LD   DE,LBHDR   
                              LD   A,10   
                              CALL   bdosx   
                              LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
                              INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
                              ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
                              LD   L,A   
                              LD   (HL),13   
01DB                          ENDIF      
01DB                          IFN   CPM   
01DB                             ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
01DB                             ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
01DB                             ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
01DB                             ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
01DB                             ; a full line.
01DB   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
01DE   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
01DF   9F                     SBC   A,A   
01E0   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
01E1   2F                     CPL      
01E2   57                     LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
01E3                             ;   at most
01E3   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
01E6   CD 0D 03     LN2:      CALL   getk   
01E9   28 FB                  JR   Z,ln2   
01EB   FE 0D                  CP   13   
01ED   28 16                  JR   Z,ln5   
01EF   FE 08                  CP   8   
01F1   28 0B                  JR   Z,ln4   
01F3   5F                     LD   E,A   
01F4   7D                     LD   A,L   
01F5   BA                     CP   D   
01F6   28 EE                  JR   Z,ln2   ; full
01F8   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01F9   2C                     INC   L   
01FA   7B                     LD   A,E   
01FB   EF           LN3:      RST   28h   
01FC   18 E8                  JR   ln2   
01FE   2D           LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
01FF   FA FB 01               JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
0202   2C                     INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
0203   18 E1                  JR   ln2   
0205   77           LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
0206                          ENDIF      
0206   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0208   F7                     RST   30h   
0209                             ; =============================================================================
0209                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
0209                             ; =============================================================================
0209                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
0209                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
0209                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
0209                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0209   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
020A   EE 02                  XOR   2   
020C   B2                     OR   D   
020D   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
020F   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
0211   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
0213   8F                     ADC   A,A   
0214   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
0215   C9                     RET      
0216   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
0217   4D                     LD   C,L   
0218   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
021B   06 10                  LD   B,16   
021D   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
021F   17                     RLA      
0220   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
0222   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
0224   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
0226   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
0227   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
0228   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
0229   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
022B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
022C   67                     LD   H,A   
022D   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
022E   C9                     RET      
022F                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
022F                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
022F   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
0232   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
0233   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0235   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0237   D0                     RET   NC   
0238   03                     INC   BC   
0239   54                     LD   D,H   
023A   5D                     LD   E,L   
023B   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
023C   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
023D   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
023E   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
023F   5F                     LD   E,A   
0240   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0242   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0243   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
0245                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
0245                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
0245                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INC   BC   
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   Z,ss0   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              RET      
0245                          ENDIF      
0245                          IF   CHECKED   
0245                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
0245                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
0245   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
0246   B7                     OR   A   
0247   C8                     RET   Z   
0248   03                     INC   BC   
0249   FE 22                  CP   22h   
024B   C8                     RET   Z   
024C   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
024E   20 F5                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0250   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
0251   B7                     OR   A   
0252   C8                     RET   Z   
0253   03                     INC   BC   
0254   18 EF                  JR   skipstr   
0256                          ENDIF      
0256                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
0256                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
0256                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
0256                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
0256                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
0256                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
0256                             ; 
0256                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
0256                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
0256                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
0256                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
0256                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
0256                SKIP:        
0256                          IF   CHECKED   
0256   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0257   DD E1                  POP   IX   
0259   0B                     DEC   BC   
025A   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
025B   03                     INC   BC   
025C   5F                     LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
025D                          ENDIF      
025D   16 00                  LD   D,0   
025F   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0260   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0261                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INC   BC   
                              OR   A   
                              JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
0261                          ENDIF      
0261                          IF   CHECKED   
0261   B7                     OR   A   
0262   28 22                  JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
0264   03                     INC   BC   
0265                          ENDIF      
0265   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0267   CC 45 02               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
026A   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
026C   28 F1                  JR   Z,sk3   
026E   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
026F   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
0271   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
0273   28 EA                  JR   Z,sk3   
0275   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
0277   20 E7                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0279   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
027A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
                              JR   sk1   
027A                          ENDIF      
027A                          IF   CHECKED   
027A   20 E4                  JR   NZ,sk1   
027C   57                     LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
027D   AB                     XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
027E   E6 06                  AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
0280   FE 02                  CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
0282   7A                     LD   A,D   
0283   C0                     RET   NZ   
0284   18 05                  JR   sk7   
0286   CB 53        SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
0288   C2 BC 04               JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
028B   DD E5        SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
028D   C1                     POP   BC   
028E   3E 4E                  LD   A,"N"   
0290   C3 7D 03               JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0293                          ENDIF      
0293                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0293   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
0295   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
0297   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
0299   EF                     RST   28h   
029A   E7                     RST   20h   
029B                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
029B                             ; Uses BC.
029B   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
029E   CD 09 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
02A1   7B                     LD   A,E   
02A2   F5                     PUSH   AF   
02A3   7C                     LD   A,H   
02A4   B5                     OR   L   
02A5   C4 9B 02               CALL   NZ,pdec   
02A8   F1                     POP   AF   
02A9   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
02AB   EF                     RST   28h   
02AC   C9                     RET      
02AD                             ; =============================================================================
02AD                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
02AD                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
02AD                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
02AD                             ; =============================================================================
02AD                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
02AD                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
02AD                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
02AD                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
02AD                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
02AD                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
02AD                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
02AD                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
02AD                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
02AD                          IF   1-TABP0   
02AD                PTAB:        
02AD                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
02AD   9C                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
02AE   A4                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
02AF   B8                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
02B0   AF                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
02B1   94                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
02B2   37                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
02B3   B5                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
02B4   13                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
02B5   1B                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
02B6   58                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
02B7   2E                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
02B8   D6                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
02B9   26                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
02BA   96                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
02BB   6C                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
02BC   92                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
02BD   9B                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
02BE   3F                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
02BF   4E                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
02C0   40                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
02C1   BE                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
02C2   0E                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
02C3   EA                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
02C4   DD                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
02C5   D9                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
02C6   72                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
02C7   85                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
02C8   C3                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
02C9   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
02CA   7A                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
02CB   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
02CC   82                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
02CD                PTABEND:      
02CD                          ENDIF      
02CD                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
02CD                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
02CD                             ; return with the carry clear.
02CD   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
02CE   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
02D0   FE 0A                  CP   10   
02D2   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
02D4   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
02D6   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
02D8   FE 06                  CP   6   
02DA   D0                     RET   NC   
02DB   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
02DD   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
02DE   C9                     RET      
02DF                             ; =============================================================================
02DF                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
02DF                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
02DF                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
02DF                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
02DF                             ; 
02DF                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
02DF                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
02DF                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
02DF                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
02DF                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
02DF                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
02DF                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
02DF                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
02DF                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
02DF                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
02DF                             ;  data stack.
02DF                             ; =============================================================================
02DF                          IFN   CPM   
02DF                RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
02DF                          ENDIF      
02DF                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
02DF   CD 06 FF     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
02E2   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
02E3   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
02E6   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
02E8   C0                     RET   NZ   
02E9                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
02E9                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
02E9                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
02E9                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
02E9   3A 7B 82     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
02EC   B7                     OR   A   
02ED   CA 75 03     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
02F0   D5                     PUSH   DE   
02F1   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
02F4   CD 06 FF     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
02F7   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
02F9   1B                     DEC   DE   
02FA   7A                     LD   A,D   
02FB   B3                     OR   E   
02FC   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
02FE   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
02FF   FE 03                  CP   3   
0301   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
0303   B7                     OR   A   
0304   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
0306   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
0309   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
030B   B7                     OR   A   
030C   C9                     RET      
030D                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
030D   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
030E   21 7A 82               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
0311   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0312   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
0314   E1                     POP   HL   
0315   B7                     OR   A   
0316   C0                     RET   NZ   
0317   CD 06 FF               CALL   rawk   
031A   C8                     RET   Z   
031B   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
031D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
031D                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
031D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
031D                          ENDIF      
031D                          IF   CHECKED   
031D                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
031D                          ENDIF      
031D                          IF   CPM   
                    RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
                                 ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
                                 ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
                    PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,6   
                              CALL   bdosx   
                              POP   HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              OR   A   ; (for getk)
                              RET      
                                 ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
                    BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
                              EXX      
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EXX      
                              LD   C,A   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              EXX      
                              POP   HL   
                              EXX      
                              POP   BC   
                              RET      
031D                          ENDIF      
031D                             ; =============================================================================
031D                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
031D                             ; =============================================================================
031D                          IF   CHECKED   
031D                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
031D                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
031D                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
031D                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
031D                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
031D                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
031D                             ; Keeps HL and BC.
031D   23           CHKST:    INC   HL   
031E   7C                     LD   A,H   
031F   2B                     DEC   HL   
0320   FE 82                  CP   LETPAGE   
0322   38 03                  JR   C,chs1   
0324                          ENDIF      
0324                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
0324   FE F0                  CP   HEAPLIM   
0326   D8                     RET   C   
0327                          ENDIF      
0327                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   E   
                              RET   NC   
0327                          ENDIF      
0327                          IF   CHECKED   
0327   C3 7B 03     CHS1:     JP   e_store   
032A                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
032A                             ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
032A                             ; program's end.
032A                CHKHP:       
032A                          ENDIF      
032A                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
                                 ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
                              RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
                              ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   H   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
032A                          ENDIF      
032A                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
032A                             ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
032A                             ; round always falls outside it.)
032A   7C                     LD   A,H   
032B   FE F0                  CP   HEAPLIM   
032D   30 09                  JR   NC,e_heap   
032F                          ENDIF      
032F                          IF   CHECKED   
032F   D5                     PUSH   DE   
0330   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0331   2A 38 82               LD   HL,(NPEND)   
0334   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
0335   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0336   D1                     POP   DE   
0337   D8                     RET   C   
0338   B7           E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
0339   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
033B   C3 78 03               JP   e_heap1   
033E                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
033E                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
033E                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
033E                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
033E                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
033E                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
033E   EB           CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
033F   21 05 7E               LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
0342   39                     ADD   HL,SP   
0343   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0344   38 1E                  JR   C,e_under   
0346   14                     INC   D   
0347   20 17                  JR   NZ,e_over   
0349   D9                     EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
034A   7C                     LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
034B   FE 80                  CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
034D   7D                     LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
034E   D9                     EXX      
034F   20 0C                  JR   NZ,e_rover   
0351   FE E1                  CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
0353   D8                     RET   C   
0354   D9                     EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
0355   21 E0 80               LD   HL,RSTOP   
0358   D9                     EXX      
0359   3E 72                  LD   A,"r"   
035B   18 20                  JR   errp   
035D   3E 52        E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
035F   11                     DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
0360   3E 53        E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
0362   18 19                  JR   errp   
0364   31 FC 81     E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
0367   3E 73                  LD   A,"s"   
0369   18 22                  JR   error   
036B                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
036B                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
036B                             ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
036B                             ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
036B   04           E_HI:     INC   B   
036C   10 17                  DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
036E   CF                     RST   08h   
036F   42                     LD   B,D   
0370   4B                     LD   C,E   
0371   3E 55                  LD   A,"U"   
0373   18 18                  JR   error   
0375                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
0375                             ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
0375   3E 42        E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
0377   11                     DB   11h   
0378   3E 48        E_HEAP1:   LD   A,"H"   ; heap (found inside chkhp)
037A   11                     DB   11h   
037B   3E 4F        E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space (chkst)
037D                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
037D   D1           ERRP:     POP   DE   
037E   18 0D                  JR   error   
0380   44           E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
0381   4D                     LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
0382   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
0384   11                     DB   11h   
0385   3E 58        E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
0387   11                     DB   11h   
0388   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
038A   11                     DB   11h   
038B   3E 57        E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
038D                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
038D                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
038D                             ; 
038D                             ;   Err X @ line,col
038D                             ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
038D                             ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
038D                             ;   Rtn n
038D   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
038E   5F                     LD   E,A   
038F   CD 62 04               CALL   pnl   
0392   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
0397   7B                     LD   A,E   
0398   EF                     RST   28h   
0399   CD 68 04               CALL   pmsg   
039C   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
03A0   0B                     DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
03A1                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
03A1                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
03A1                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
03A1   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
03A4   11 00 00               LD   DE,0   
03A7   78                     LD   A,B   
03A8   FE 83                  CP   PROG/256   
03AA   38 14                  JR   C,er3   
03AC   24                     INC   H   
03AD   6B                     LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
03AE   13           ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
03AF   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03B0   7D           ER2:      LD   A,L   
03B1   91                     SUB   C   
03B2   7C                     LD   A,H   
03B3   98                     SBC   A,B   
03B4   30 09                  JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
03B6   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
03B7   23                     INC   HL   
03B8   FE 0A                  CP   10   
03BA   20 F4                  JR   NZ,er2   
03BC   F1                     POP   AF   
03BD   18 EF                  JR   er1   
03BF   E1           ER2X:     POP   HL   
03C0   C5           ER3:      PUSH   BC   
03C1   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03C2   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
03C3   CD 9B 02               CALL   pdec   ; the line
03C6   3E 2C                  LD   A,","   
03C8   EF                     RST   28h   
03C9   D1                     POP   DE   
03CA   E1                     POP   HL   
03CB   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03CC   B7                     OR   A   
03CD   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
03CF   23                     INC   HL   
03D0   CD 9B 02               CALL   pdec   ; the column
03D3   CD 62 04               CALL   pnl   
03D6   22                     DB   22h   
03D7   E1                     POP   HL   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
03D8   06 10                  LD   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
03DA   7E           ER4:      LD   A,(HL)   
03DB   23                     INC   HL   
03DC   B7                     OR   A   
03DD   28 0B                  JR   Z,er5   
03DF   FE 0D                  CP   13   
03E1   28 07                  JR   Z,er5   
03E3   FE 0A                  CP   10   
03E5   28 03                  JR   Z,er5   
03E7                          ENDIF      
03E7                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              CP   1Ah   ; (the ^Z that pads a file's last record ends
                              JR   Z,er5   ;   the text too: some terminals clear the
03E7                          ENDIF      ;   screen on it)
03E7                          IF   CHECKED   
03E7   EF                     RST   28h   
03E8   10 F0                  DJNZ   er4   
03EA                ER5:         ; (without the editor: on into pstk)
03EA                          ENDIF      
03EA                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
03EA   CD F4 03               CALL   pstk   
03ED   CD 62 04               CALL   pnl   
03F0   22                     DB   22h   
03F1   C3 B8 04               JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
03F4                          ENDIF      
03F4                             ; =============================================================================
03F4                             ;  Routines that the checked build's report and the editor share
03F4                             ; =============================================================================
03F4                SPADJ:    EQU   2*EDITOR   ; (with the editor pstk is called, not fallen
03F4                             ;   into: the stack is one address deeper)
03F4                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
03F4                             ; pstk: the two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
03F4                             ;                             Rtn n
03F4                             ; TOS must be in memory with the rest (pushed). In a build without the
03F4                             ; editor this is the end of `error`, which runs on into it.
03F4   CD 62 04     PSTK:     CALL   pnl   
03F7   53 74 6B 20 22         DB   "Stk ",22h   
03FC   21 F8 81               LD   HL,DSTOP-2-SPADJ   ; (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed with the
03FF   B7                     OR   A   ;   first value and holds nothing)
0400   ED 72                  SBC   HL,SP   
0402   CD 45 04               CALL   phalf   ; the depth
0405   3E 3A                  LD   A,":"   
0407   EF                     RST   28h   
0408   79                     LD   A,C   
0409   FE 09                  CP   9   
040B   38 0A                  JR   C,er6   
040D   CD 68 04               CALL   pmsg   
0410   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
0415   0E 08                  LD   C,8   
0417   26 00        ER6:      LD   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
0419   69                     LD   L,C   
041A   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
041B   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
041C                          ENDIF      
041C                          IF   EDITOR   
041C   23                     INC   HL   
041D   23                     INC   HL   
041E                          ENDIF      
041E                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
041E   0C                     INC   C   
041F   0D           ER7:      DEC   C   
0420   28 11                  JR   Z,er8   
0422   2B                     DEC   HL   
0423   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0424   2B                     DEC   HL   
0425   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
0426   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0427   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0428   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
042A   EF                     RST   28h   
042B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
042C   CD 93 02               CALL   psgn   
042F   C1                     POP   BC   
0430   E1                     POP   HL   
0431   18 EC                  JR   er7   
0433   CD 62 04     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
0436   52 74 6E 20 22         DB   "Rtn ",22h   
043B   D9                     EXX      
043C   E5                     PUSH   HL   
043D   D9                     EXX      
043E   D1                     POP   DE   
043F   21 E0 80               LD   HL,RSTOP   
0442   B7                     OR   A   
0443   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0445                          ENDIF      
0445                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              CALL   phalf   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   endprog   
0445                          ENDIF      
0445                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0445                             ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C. (With the editor, pstk ends by
0445                             ; running on into this.)
0445   CB 3C        PHALF:    SRL   H   
0447   CB 1D                  RR   L   
0449   E5                     PUSH   HL   
044A   CD 9B 02               CALL   pdec   
044D   C1                     POP   BC   
044E   C9                     RET      
044F                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
044F                             ; "$", and the texts of the report and the editor). In the checked build a
044F                             ; NUL first is an error: Q.
044F   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
0450   23                     INC   HL   
0451   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0453   C8                     RET   Z   
0454                          ENDIF      
0454                          IF   CHECKED   
0454   B7                     OR   A   
0455   28 17                  JR   Z,e_dollar   
0457                          ENDIF      
0457                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0457   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0459   20 04                  JR   NZ,prs1   
045B   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
045C   23                     INC   HL   
045D   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
045F   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
0460   18 ED                  JR   prstr   
0462                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
0462                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
0462   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
0464   EF                     RST   28h   
0465   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0467   EF                     RST   28h   
0468   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
0469   CD 4F 04               CALL   prstr   
046C   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
046D   C9                     RET      
046E                          ENDIF      
046E                          IF   CHECKED   
046E   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
046F   E1                     POP   HL   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
0470   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
0472   C3 8D 03               JP   error   
0475                          ENDIF      
0475                             ; =============================================================================
0475                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
0475                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
0475                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
0475                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
0475                             ;    n         take line n out
0475                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
0475                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;    ^G        run the program
0475                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
0475                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
0475                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
0475                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
0475                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
0475                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
0475                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
0475                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
0475                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
0475                             ;    ^V        view: the build, both stacks, and the program's size, lines
0475                             ;              and free memory
0475                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
0475                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
0475                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
0475                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
0475                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
0475                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
0475                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
0475                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
0475                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
0475                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;  Things to know:
0475                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
0475                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
0475                             ;      after editing it.
0475                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
0475                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
0475                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
0475                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
0475                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
0475                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
0475                             ; 
0475                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
0475                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
0475                             ; =============================================================================
0475                          IF   EDGEN   
0475                INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
0475                          ENDIF      
0475                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
0475                             ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
0475                             ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
0475                             ; (see e_hi).
0475   21 00 82               LD   HL,LET   
0478   77           INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
0479   2C                     INC   L   
047A   F2 78 04               JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
047D                          ENDIF      
047D                          IF   EDGEN   
047D   18 39                  JR   edit0   
047F                          ENDIF      
047F                          IF   EDITOR   
047F                             ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
047F   7D           LEFT:     LD   A,L   
0480   87                     ADD   A,A   
0481   28 4D                  JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
0483   2D                     DEC   L   
0484   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
0486   EF           LF1:      RST   28h   
0487   18 47                  JR   ed1   
0489                             ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
0489   7D           RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
048A   BB                     CP   E   
048B   28 43                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
048D   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
048E   2C                     INC   L   
048F   18 F5                  JR   lf1   
0491                             ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
0491                             ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
0491                             ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
0491   01 C8 00     ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
0494   CD 06 FF     ES1:      CALL   rawk   
0497   20 0A                  JR   NZ,es2   
0499   0B                     DEC   BC   
049A   78                     LD   A,B   
049B   B1                     OR   C   
049C   20 F6                  JR   NZ,es1   
049E   CD 05 05               CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
04A1   18 1B                  JR   edit   
04A3   FE 5B        ES2:      CP   "["   
04A5   20 29                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
04A7   CD 5E 05     ES3:      CALL   ekey   
04AA   FE 40                  CP   40h   
04AC   38 F9                  JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
04AE   FE 43                  CP   "C"   
04B0   28 D7                  JR   Z,right   
04B2   FE 44                  CP   "D"   
04B4   28 C9                  JR   Z,left   
04B6   18 18                  JR   ed1   
04B8                             ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
04B8                             ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
04B8                             ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
04B8   31 FA 81     EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
04BB   21                     DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
04BC   D1           SKEND:    POP   DE   
04BD   E5           EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
04BE                             ; edit: start a new input line.
04BE   D9           EDIT:     EXX      
04BF   21 E0 80               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
04C2   D9                     EXX      
04C3   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
04C6   22 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
04C9   22 3A 82               LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
04CC   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
04CF   5D                     LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
04D0   CD 5E 05     ED1:      CALL   ekey   
04D3   FE 7F                  CP   7Fh   
04D5   28 40                  JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
04D7   FE 20                  CP   " "   
04D9   30 56                  JR   NC,insc   
04DB   FE 09                  CP   9   
04DD   28 52                  JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
04DF   FE 08                  CP   8   
04E1   28 34                  JR   Z,bsp   
04E3   FE 02                  CP   2   
04E5   28 98                  JR   Z,left   ; ^B
04E7   FE 06                  CP   6   
04E9   28 9E                  JR   Z,right   ; ^F
04EB   FE 1B                  CP   1Bh   
04ED   28 A2                  JR   Z,esc   
04EF   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
04F0   21 64 05               LD   HL,cmds   
04F3   06 09                  LD   B,NCMD   
04F5   BE           ED2:      CP   (HL)   
04F6   23                     INC   HL   
04F7   28 07                  JR   Z,ed3   
04F9   23                     INC   HL   
04FA   23                     INC   HL   
04FB   10 F8                  DJNZ   ed2   
04FD   E1                     POP   HL   
04FE   18 D0                  JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
0500   7E           ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
0501   23                     INC   HL   
0502   66                     LD   H,(HL)   
0503   6F                     LD   L,A   
0504   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
0505                             ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
0505                             ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
0505   26 82        FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
0507   6B                     LD   L,E   
0508   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
050A   2C                     INC   L   
050B   36 0A                  LD   (HL),10   
050D   2D                     DEC   L   
050E   CD DC 06               CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
0511   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
0513   01 80 82               LD   BC,LINEBUF   
0516   C9                     RET      
0517                             ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
0517                             ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
0517                             ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
0517   7D           BSP:      LD   A,L   
0518   87                     ADD   A,A   
0519   28 B5                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
051B   2D                     DEC   L   
051C   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
051E   EF                     RST   28h   
051F   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0520   2C           BS1:      INC   L   
0521   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0522   2D                     DEC   L   
0523   77                     LD   (HL),A   
0524   2C                     INC   L   
0525   7D                     LD   A,L   
0526   BB                     CP   E   
0527   20 F7                  JR   NZ,bs1   
0529   2D                     DEC   L   
052A   36 20                  LD   (HL)," "   
052C   E1                     POP   HL   
052D   53                     LD   D,E   
052E   1D                     DEC   E   
052F   18 15                  JR   ic2   
0531                             ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
0531                             ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
0531   47           INSC:     LD   B,A   
0532   7B                     LD   A,E   
0533   FE FD                  CP   0FDh   
0535   28 99                  JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
0537   78                     LD   A,B   
0538   EF                     RST   28h   
0539   E5                     PUSH   HL   
053A   7E           IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
053B   70                     LD   (HL),B   
053C   47                     LD   B,A   
053D   7D                     LD   A,L   
053E   2C                     INC   L   
053F   BB                     CP   E   
0540   20 F8                  JR   NZ,ic1   
0542   E1                     POP   HL   
0543   2C                     INC   L   
0544   1C                     INC   E   
0545   53                     LD   D,E   
0546   CD 4B 05     IC2:      CALL   tail   
0549   18 85                  JR   ed1   
054B                             ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
054B                             ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
054B   4D           TAIL:     LD   C,L   
054C   7D           TA1:      LD   A,L   
054D   BA                     CP   D   
054E   28 05                  JR   Z,ta2   
0550   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0551   EF                     RST   28h   
0552   2C                     INC   L   
0553   18 F7                  JR   ta1   
0555   7D           TA2:      LD   A,L   
0556   B9                     CP   C   
0557   C8                     RET   Z   
0558   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
055A   EF                     RST   28h   
055B   2D                     DEC   L   
055C   18 F7                  JR   ta2   
055E                             ; ekey: wait for a key
055E   CD 06 FF     EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
0561   28 FB                  JR   Z,ekey   
0563   C9                     RET      
0564                             ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
0564   0D           CMDS:     DB   13   
0565   BE 05                  DW   cret   
0567   07                     DB   7   ; ^G
0568   06 06                  DW   crun   
056A   0C                     DB   12   ; ^L
056B   1C 06                  DW   clist   
056D   05                     DB   5   ; ^E
056E   8D 05                  DW   cedln   
0570   12                     DB   18   ; ^R
0571   E5 06                  DW   cread   
0573   17                     DB   23   ; ^W
0574   18 07                  DW   cwrite   
0576   0E                     DB   14   ; ^N
0577   7F 05                  DW   cnew   
0579   16                     DB   22   ; ^V
057A   4E 06                  DW   cview   
057C   18                     DB   24   ; ^X
057D   09 FF                  DW   LEAVE   
057F                NCMD:     EQU   9   
057F                             ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
057F   CD 5E 05     CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
0582   FE 0E                  CP   14   
0584   20 04                  JR   NZ,ged0   
0586   AF                     XOR   A   
0587   32 00 83               LD   (PROG),A   
058A   C3 BE 04     GED0:     JP   edit   
058D                             ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
058D                             ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
058D   CD 2F 02     CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
0590   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0591   CD C4 06               CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
0594   D1                     POP   DE   
0595   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0596   B7                     OR   A   
0597   28 F1                  JR   Z,ged0   
0599   ED 53 3A 82            LD   (EDLN),DE   
059D   11 80 82               LD   DE,LINEBUF   
05A0   7E           CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
05A1   FE 0D                  CP   13   
05A3   28 0C                  JR   Z,ce2   
05A5   FE 0A                  CP   10   
05A7   28 08                  JR   Z,ce2   
05A9   12                     LD   (DE),A   
05AA   23                     INC   HL   
05AB   1C                     INC   E   
05AC   7B                     LD   A,E   
05AD   FE FD                  CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
05AF   20 EF                  JR   NZ,ce1   
05B1   21 80 82     CE2:      LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; show it; the cursor ends up at its end
05B4   7D           CE3:      LD   A,L   
05B5   BB                     CP   E   
05B6   CA D0 04               JP   Z,ed1   
05B9   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
05BA   EF                     RST   28h   
05BB   2C                     INC   L   
05BC   18 F6                  JR   ce3   
05BE                             ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
05BE                             ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
05BE                             ; and anything else is run where it is.
05BE   E5           CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
05BF   2A 3A 82               LD   HL,(EDLN)   
05C2   7C                     LD   A,H   
05C3   B5                     OR   L   
05C4   28 07                  JR   Z,cr1   
05C6   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05C7   CD B4 06               CALL   delln   
05CA   E1                     POP   HL   
05CB   18 13                  JR   ins   
05CD   CD 2F 02     CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
05D0   79                     LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
05D1   87                     ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
05D2   28 36                  JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
05D4   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
05D5   FE 0D                  CP   13   
05D7   20 06                  JR   NZ,cr2   
05D9   D1                     POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
05DA   CD B4 06               CALL   delln   
05DD   18 24                  JR   gedit   
05DF   03           CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
05E0                             ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
05E0                             ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
05E0   CD C4 06     INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
05E3   D1                     POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
05E4   7B                     LD   A,E   
05E5   91                     SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
05E6   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the text
05E7   4F                     LD   C,A   
05E8   06 00                  LD   B,0   
05EA   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; its length
05EB   54                     LD   D,H   
05EC   5D                     LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
05ED   AF                     XOR   A   
05EE   4F                     LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
05EF   ED B1                  CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
05F1   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
05F3   44                     LD   B,H   
05F4   4D                     LD   C,L   
05F5   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
05F6   2B                     DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
05F7   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05F8   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
05F9   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05FA   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
05FB   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05FC   ED B8                  LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
05FE   C1                     POP   BC   ; the length
05FF   D1                     POP   DE   ; where it goes
0600   E1                     POP   HL   ; the text
0601   ED B0                  LDIR      
0603   C3 BE 04     GEDIT:    JP   edit   
0606                             ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
0606   01 00 83     CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
0609   3E                     DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
060A   E1           ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
060B                             ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
060B   21 00 83     ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
060E   AF                     XOR   A   
060F   BE           ST1:      CP   (HL)   
0610   23                     INC   HL   
0611   20 FC                  JR   NZ,st1   
